Maintainer: Kwame AMEDODJI <kwame-externe.amedodji@edf.fr>
Build-Depends: debhelper (>= 10), libslurm-dev (>= 25.05)
Standards-Version: 3.9.8

Package: slurm-spank-plugin-ebpf
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, systemd
Description: Slurm SPANK plugin driving ebpf_exporter over a job lifetime
 This SPANK plugin starts ebpf_exporter on a compute node when a job begins
 and stops it once no job needs it anymore, so eBPF probes are only loaded
 while real work is running instead of permanently across the cluster.
 .
 A reference counter in /run/ebpf_exporter.refcount, guarded with flock(),
 keeps concurrent jobs on the same node consistent: the exporter starts on
 the first prolog and stops on the last epilog.
 .
 Two modes are selected from plugstack.conf: "always" enables the exporter
 for every job, "opt-in" restricts it to jobs submitted with --ebpf. Opt-in
 mode needs the package installed on submission hosts too, see
 /usr/share/doc/slurm-spank-plugin-ebpf/README.Debian.
